.TH CLAYMORE 1 "September 2026" "Claymore@Linux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claymore \- lighting control for the ASUS ROG Claymore keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claymore
.I command
[
.IR options ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claymore
drives the lighting of an ASUS ROG Claymore (USB 0b05:184d) from Linux, either
through the built in firmware effects or frame by frame in direct mode.
It talks to the keyboard through
.I /dev/hidraw
and depends on nothing beyond libc.
.PP
Run it without arguments, or with
.BR help ,
for the same list of commands as below.
.SH DEVICE COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every hidraw node and mark which one is the keyboard.
.TP
.B info
Firmware version, which side the numpad is on, the key legends and the layout
in use.
.TP
.B keys
Every key, with its frame slot and its device LED index.
.TP
.B layout
An ASCII map of the active layout. With
.B --list
it names the layout variants instead.
.SH LIGHTING COMMANDS
.TP
.BI effect " name"
Apply a firmware effect:
.BR static ", " breathing ", " color-cycle ", " reactive ", " wave ", "
.BR ripple ", " starry-night ", " quicksand ", " current " or " rain-drop .
See
.B "EFFECTS, SPEEDS AND BRIGHTNESS"
below.
.TP
.BI preset " id"
Apply one of the built in presets;
.B presets
lists them.
.TP
.BI static " colour"
Shortcut for
.BR "effect static" .
.TP
.B off
Shortcut for
.BR "static black" .
.TP
.B paint
Compose
.I one
frame in direct mode, in a single session, which is what makes per-key work
possible at all: each command line invocation is a separate process, and
granting direct mode twice leaves only the second frame lit. Options may be
combined freely:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-all " colour"
Fill every key.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " name=colour"
Repaint one key; repeat for as many keys as you like.
.TP
.BI \-\-design " file"
Load a design saved by the graphical interface.
.TP
.B \-\-default
Load the design marked as the startup design.
.RE
.TP
.BI set " slot|key colour"
Repaint a single key. Blanks every other key, so use
.B paint
for anything more than one key.
.TP
.BI fill " colour"
Paint the whole board in direct mode.
.TP
.B release
Hand the keyboard back to its own firmware effects.
.TP
.B reset
Release, then apply a firmware effect.
.TP
.BI preview " effect"
Animate an effect in the terminal. Needs no keyboard.
.SH DESIGN COMMANDS
.TP
.B designs
List saved designs, marking the one applied at login.
.TP
.BI default " name"
Choose the design a login should apply, or
.B none
to stop doing so.
.SH PREFERENCES
.TP
.B settings
List the preferences shared with the graphical interface.
.TP
.BI settings " name value"
Change one. The only setting with a meaning of its own is
.BR start-in-tray ,
which the graphical interface reads at launch:
.RS
.PP
.EX
claymore settings start-in-tray on
.EE
.RE
.PP
With it on, the window stays away and only the panel icon appears, which is
what an autostart entry wants.
.B claymore-gui --window
opens a window anyway for one run.
.SH SYNC DAEMON
.TP
.B syncd
Hold the keyboard in direct mode and let any process stream frames over a UNIX
datagram socket, the Linux stand in for Aura Sync. Options:
.BR \-\-socket " path,"
.BR \-\-fps " n,"
.BR \-\-demo ","
.BR \-\-stdin ","
.BR \-\-idle-effect " name,"
.BR \-\-idle-timeout " ms."
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-color " RRGGBB|name"
Add a colour; repeatable. The name
.B off
means black.
.TP
.B \-\-random
Let the firmware pick colours at random.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " 0-100"
Animation speed, 100 being fastest. Each effect starts at the speed ASUS ships
for it.
.TP
.BI \-\-brightness " 0-3"
Firmware light level. Experimental: the byte is undocumented.
.TP
.BI \-\-direction " lr|rl|up|down"
Direction for the effects that have one.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " path"
Use a particular hidraw node instead of detecting one.
.TP
.BI \-\-vid " hex" " \fR,\fP " \-\-pid " hex"
Match different USB identifiers.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " n"
HID interface number; the default, 1, is where the Claymore keeps its lighting
control collection.
.TP
.BI \-\-usage-page " hex"
HID usage page; the default is 0xff00.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " id"
Force a layout variant;
.B "layout \-\-list"
names them.
.TP
.BI \-\-region " us|uk"
Override the detected key legends.
.TP
.BI \-\-numpad " none|left|right"
Override the detected numpad side.
.TP
.BI \-\-ack-timeout " ms"
How long to wait for the keyboard to acknowledge a report. The default, 20, is
plenty for effects; streaming direct mode frames needs a much shorter one,
which
.B syncd
sets for itself.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress messages.
.SH EFFECTS, SPEEDS AND BRIGHTNESS
A colour effect needs at least one
.BR \-\-color .
Effects without a direction ignore
.BR \-\-direction ,
and static ignores
.BR \-\-speed .
.PP
Speed is linear in the firmware byte, and the fastest end is 0, so the two
scales run in opposite directions; the percentages shown are converted before
they are sent.
.SH STORING EFFECTS
The keyboard needs the 0x50 0x55 commit packet to display an effect at all:
without it the board flashes the new effect and then reverts to the previous
one. Every effect change is therefore stored in the keyboard's flash, and
.B \-\-no-save
is accepted but ignored. See
.IR docs/PROTOCOL.md
for why.
.SH DESIGNS
A painted design is not an effect, and the keyboard cannot store one: its flash
holds built in effects only. What it does do is keep the last frame it is
given, so
.B paint
leaves the design on the board without revoking remote control, and it stays
lit with nothing running.
.B release
hands the board back.
.PP
A design lives in
.RI ~/.config/claymore/designs/ name .txt
as one
.I "slot colour"
line per key, so it is diffable, hand editable and scriptable. The design to
apply at login is recorded in
.IR ~/.config/claymore/default-design ,
which
.B "claymore paint --default"
reads.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claymore/settings
Preferences, one
.I "name value"
per line.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claymore/designs/
Saved designs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claymore/default-design
The design name to apply at login.
.TP
.I /usr/share/udev/rules.d/99-claymore-linux.rules
Installed by the package; grants members of
.B plugdev
access to the hidraw node so the tool can run without root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, with a message on standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
claymore info
claymore effect wave --color ff003c --color 00c8ff --direction left
claymore paint --all 002060 --key escape=ff003c
claymore paint --default
claymore release
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claymore-gui (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/claymore-linux/PROTOCOL.md
